---
epr-meta-version: 1
id: k8s-runtime-envelope-render
purpose: >
  Pure outward resource translation for the orchestrator; manifests declare, Kubernetes renders.
rules:
  - id: manifest-render-contract
    class: inject
    when: { write: "*.rs" }
    dedupe-of: "bridges/k8s/tests/contracts.rs"
    why: >
      Reuse RuntimeManifest::cid for identity. Keep absent envelopes empty and split arithmetic
      byte-equal to conductor-split-budget.sh. 2026-09-05: all seven active humans are pinned,
      so Unpinned has graduated from refer to refuse (CLI exit 65). Rendering is not enforcement.
---

# Runtime envelope bridge

The consumer is the orchestrator through the k8s-bridge CLI. No network, DHT anchoring,
cgroup enforcement, capacity promotion, or volume-head semantics are implemented here.
The dated Unpinned refusal is exercised by cli_missing_pin_refuses and the pre-push leg.
